      "text": "my 44 year old friend, did $340,000 from YouTube this year and he doesn't own a f**cking channel, no subscribers, no social media presence, nothing!!!!\n\nyet he makes more on YouTube than niggas grinding their ass to post the next viral LONGFORM\n\nHe leaked everything to me.\n\nand he called it the REVERSE EFFECT OF TRUMPETING.\n\nhe didn't have influencers shout out his stuff.\n\nHe did none of that.\n\nYet, he kept siphoning leads out of YouTube.\n\nI'm in a good mood, so I'll leak everything.\n\nInternet YT in 2025 is a fallacy.\n\nwhilst everyone is grinding, recording, editing, and trying to get monetized off YouTube.\n\nThere are soft niggas who never show themselves on the internet, yet they make more than those parading everyday for attention.\n\nhere's the playbook you never understood ↓\n\ncurrently 90% of YT videos posted are dumbsh*t.\n\nYou have a creator desperate for winning the algorithm.\n\nPosting 1 hour BS in the name of “VALUE”\n\nEvery single video looks great, but at the end the viewers leave unsatisfied, tired and searching for the next solution on the YT search.\n\npeople hardly watch educational YouTube videos.\n\nwhat they do is this ↓\n\n➼ Get stuck in a problem or task, probably business issue, finance platforms, selling to a client who's Skeptical, simple but critical issues.\n\n➼ go on YouTube and search with the keyword “How to run cold emails without external assistance”\n\n➼ Scroll for tutorials\n\n➼ find one with a hooking title, fast forward ten seconds.\n\n➼ take the link and get the transcript.\n\n➼ transcript looks confusing\n\n➼ go back to the video to watch \n\n➼ video too lengthy\n\n➼ Check Comments\n\nThat's where he strikes.\n\nsomeone would post a 30 minute video: “How I Built a 6-Figure Shopify Store.”\n\nsolid content. good production. 200K views.\n\nbut every comment section told the same story:\n\n→ “great video but how do you actually find winning products?”\n\n→ “loved this but got stuck on the Facebook ads part”\n\n→ “anyone know a good supplier? he didn't mention that”\n\n→ “this worked in 2021 but doesn't Meta block this now?”\n\nthe video answered the question in the title, but created 12 new questions in the viewer's head.\n\n“creators optimize for watch time and retention. not for actually solving the problem completely. there's always a gap. that gap is where I live.”\n\n80% of decisions on the internet are validated off comments.\n\nIn comments you find people aligning, some shitting on the video, and then my friend driving Perception.\n\nHe doesn't do it.\n\nHe has a team who does it, 250 real accounts, hired people in the Philippines, paid monthly, gave them training docs on how to spot gaps, how to comment naturally. how to validate each other without being obvious.\n\nEach account\n\n➼ Follows a big page and small creators rising\n\n➼ subscribed to 400+ channels each across business, finance, health, relationships, tech tutorials.\n\n➼ Real profile picture\n\n➼ they'd screen for videos hitting 10K views in the first 48 hours. early signal.\n\n➼ Big accounts post they wait for confirmation and strike\n\n➼ Small accounts post they strike\n\n➼ All 250 real commenters are in one group, called the perception hub.\n\n➼ Videos are dropped every 9 hours\n\n➼ Commenters comment separately in 10 minutes intervals per batches of 20\n\n➼ 10% of the commenters reply to their fellow commenter to validate thoughts\n\n➼ 100% of the commenters like their fellow Commenters comments to push the comment in ranking.\n\n➼ 249 commenters like 1 comment post, vice versa\n\n➼ Comments gets pushed, anyone opening the video sees the comment first.\n\n➼ Scroll comments? You see more\n\n➼ when the same confusion of something appeared 8+ times, they moved.\n\n➼ created a micro-product in 12-18 hours. Notion template. video course module. spreadsheet. checklist. guide. whatever format fit.\nprice point: $27-$67. impulse buy range.\n\n➼ And the perception drive is created\n\nThis is how it works ↓\n\nthe comments.\n\nnot spam. not links. just organic mentions.\n\n“struggled with this exact thing for weeks, ended up using the Davidson Method breakdown (think it's on Gumroad?). it's the only thing that actually explained the tracking setup step by step.”\n\n6 other accounts would interact over the next 90 minutes.\n\n→ “what's the Davidson Method?”\n\n→ “just grabbed it. legit actually.”\n\n→ “okay but is it actually worth $50 or is it basic?”\n\n→ “I mean it's $49 and it's literally the missing piece from this video so yeah”\n\nthe comments would cluster near the top. upvoted by the team. replied to by real viewers now.\n\n“we never sell in the comment. we reference. humans trust references more than recommendations. we're not affiliates. we're not promoting. we're just people who already solved this specific problem.”\n\nHE GOT SYSTEMATIC.\n\nthey produce 6-8 micro-products a month. some flop. most break even. 2-3 hit big.\n\n“we made $38K in November on a cold email template pack for B2B sales. video had 380K views. guy spent 18 minutes on strategy but never showed his actual templates. comments were begging for examples. we made 7 templates in Notion. $39. sold 970 copies in 6 weeks.”\n\nI asked the obvious question.\n\n➼ isn't this manipulating people?\n\n“is it manipulation when the video promised a complete solution and didn't deliver? I'm solving the actual problem. I'm just better at identifying what people need than the creator was. and I don't need my face on camera to do it.”\n\nhe said most creators are too close to their content.\n\n“they think their video is complete because they covered what they think matters. but the audience tells you what actually matters. it's right there in the comments. most creators never read them.”\n\n➼ no paid ads?\n\n“never. paid ads create resistance. comments create curiosity. nobody thinks a comment is trying to sell them something.”\n\n➼ no email list?\n\n“I have a list now. 14,000 people. but it came from the products, not the other way around. I didn't build an audience first. I solved problems first. audience is a side effect.”\n\n➼ no brand?\n\n“I have 20 brands. whatever name fits the niche. Davidson Method. Chen Systems. Apex Templates. Rivera Framework. none of them are me. all of them are just signals of authority. people don't buy from people anymore. they buy from things that sound like they've already helped other people.”\n\n➼ I asked what happens when YouTube cracks down on this.\n\n“they won't. we're not violating TOS. we're not spamming. we're real accounts having real conversations. the Federal Trade Commission requires disclosure for affiliate links and sponsorships. we're not affiliates. we're customers recommending products. is that illegal? is word-of-mouth illegal now?”\n\nhe opened his notebook and showed me his tracking sheet.\n\n47 active videos being monitored. 12 products in various stages. conversion rates per niche. comment engagement scores.\n\nall handwritten!\n\n“I don't automate this part. automation makes you stupid. I read 200 comments a day myself still. that's where the insights are. that's where the money is.”\n\nWe went out, had some steaks, and I left.",
